            "notes": "Climb the 32 steep marble steps flanked by carved stone elephants to enter the city’s foremost Vishnu temple, commissioned in 1651 by Maharana Jagat Singh. Marvel at the 79-foot high spire (shikhar) adorned with friezes of musicians, dancers, and celestial beings. Pay homage to the four-armed black stone idol of Lord Jagannath (Vishnu) in the sanctum amidst soul-stirring live devotional bhajans before the 12:30 midday arti closure.",
