            "notes": "Immerse yourself in vibrant Rajasthani cultural heritage at Bagore Ki Haveli’s open-air Neem Chowk courtyard. Witness the celebrated Dharohar performance: dynamic Chari fire-dance with burning brass pots on dancers heads, Terah Taali with 13 brass cymbals tied across the body, traditional Rajasthani puppet theatrics, and the breathtaking Bhavai climax where a seasoned folk dancer balances up to 11 earthen pots on her head atop broken glass shards.",
